{"strongs": "H4321", "word": "מִיכָֽיְהוּ", "translit": "mi.kha.ye.hu", "root": "מטל", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "Micaiah", "definition": "מִיכָֽיְהוּ proper name, masculine (so on an Israel scarab, Ganneau JAS 1883, 156, No. 42 ) — 1. an Ephraimite, Judg 17:1 ; Judg 17:4 (in Judg 17:5 ff., Judg 18:2 ff called מִיכָה ). 2. a prophet, the son of Imlah ( ᵐ5 Μειχαίας ), 1Kgs 22:8-26 (9 t.), || 2Chr 18:7-25 (7 t.) + v 2Chr 18:8 Qr ( Kt מיכהו ). 3. a contemporary of Jeremiah, Jer 36:11 ( מִכָֽיְהוּ ), v Jer 36:13 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4618')\">BDB4618</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4321')\">H4321</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H4319')\">H4319</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4617')\">BDB4617</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4619')\">BDB4619</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מִיכָֽיְהוּ</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine</b> (so on an Israel scarab, Ganneau<sup>JAS 1883, 156, No. 42</sup>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> an Ephraimite, <ref ref=\"Judg 17:1\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(7,17,1)\">Judg 17:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 17:4\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(7,17,4)\">Judg 17:4</ref> (in <ref ref=\"Judg 17:5\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"17\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"17\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(7,17,5)\">Judg 17:5</ref>ff., <ref ref=\"Judg 18:2\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(7,18,2)\">Judg 18:2</ref>ff called <bdbheb>מִיכָה</bdbheb>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> a prophet, the son of Imlah (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Μειχαίας</grk>), <ref ref=\"1Kgs 22:8-26\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(11,22,8)\">1Kgs 22:8-26</ref> (9 t.), || <ref ref=\"2Chr 18:7-25\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(14